  "body": "Our owners are moving into retirement living and have given us clear instructions to sell as quickly as possible. If you've been looking for a spacious family home with privacy, plenty of off-street parking and a generous freehold section just minutes from Gulf Harbour Marina and Wentworth College, come and see what's on offer. \r\n\r\nThe home makes a strong first impression, with a generous driveway, plenty of off-street parking for a boat or campervan, and a large internal-access double garage. The arched front doorway opens into a light-filled foyer, where a wide staircase and an upper landing overlooking the entrance give the home real character.  Large windows in the sunken lounge and dining area bring the greenery into view, so you feel close to the garden even when you're indoors. A second lounge beside the kitchen gives the family another place to spread out, and both living areas open outdoors, making it easy to move between the house and garden.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, all three bedrooms are generous doubles. The main bedroom has a walk-in wardrobe, an ensuite and a bay window overlooking the garden. Downstairs, a separate study gives you a dedicated place to work from home, while the spacious kitchen has ample storage and a lovely outlook over the grounds. The garden itself is a standout. Mature planting and terraced stonework frame the grounds, and a water feature adds to the sense of calm. There's room for the kids to play, established beds for anyone who loves to garden, and enough privacy to sit outside and enjoy it all.\r\n\r\nLife in Gulf Harbour means a morning walk around the marina, coffee in the village and afternoons at the beach. Nearby Shakespear Regional Park is an easy weekend outing, with coastal tracks and sheltered bays to explore. And with the water so close, there's always time to take the kids for a swim or head out for a few hours on the boat.\r\n\r\nBe in for Christmas, our owners are ready to move now. Call Chris or Sue to arrange your viewing.\r\n\r\nProperty Documents can be downloaded here: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/WUNB",
